# JavaScript Standards

## Structure

Single `DOMContentLoaded` entry calling `init*` functions. No jQuery. No bundler.

```javascript
document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function () {
  initMobileMenu();
  initHotwPolaroidSwiper();
  // ...
});
```

## Defensive initialization

Every init must check root selector exists and return early:

```javascript
function initHotwPolaroidSwiper() {
  var root = document.querySelector(".hotw-polaroid-swiper");
  if (!root || typeof Swiper === "undefined") return;
  // ...
}
```

## Libraries

- **Swiper** — carousels; guard with `typeof Swiper === "undefined"`
- **Bootstrap 5** — modals (`shown.bs.modal`, `hidden.bs.modal`)

## Responsive Swiper pattern

Use `matchMedia("(max-width: 991.98px)")` with `change` listener to create/destroy instances.

## Naming

- Init functions: `initHotw{Feature}()` or `init{Feature}()` matching existing style
- Toggle classes: `.is-open`, `--is-active`
- ARIA: update `aria-expanded`, `aria-selected`, `hidden` attribute

## Do not add

- `console.log` in production code
- Global state without namespace
- Dependencies not enqueued in `functions.php`
